      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hartford_City%2C_West_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Colonel Andrew Waggener was awarded four thousand acres in this region by King George III in 1772 for his military service.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://wvexplorer.com/travel/communities/cities-towns/hartford-city-west-virginia/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Hartford City was established as a town in 1853, and a coal mine opened that same year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hartford_City%2C_West_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Connecticut capitalists Morgan Buckley and William Healey named the town after Hartford, the capital of Connecticut, when salt extraction began in 1856.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hartford_City%2C_West_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Hartford City is known for its historic architecture, which is most evident along the banks of the Ohio River.",
